TARGET_IDENTITY T0
  SOURCE E1
  SOURCE_STATEMENT If A subset {1,...,N} with |A|=n is such that the subset sums sum_{a in S} a are distinct for all S subset A then N >> 2^n
  SOURCE_FINGERPRINT the enriched_statement string in oracle/evidence/encirclement-quad/erdos_1_v2/S01_terminal.json
  FORMAL_STATEMENT exists C > 0, for all N and all A with IsSumDistinctSet A N and N nonzero, C * 2 ^ A.card <= N
  BINDING TRANSCRIPTION_CERT
  BINDING_WITNESS the predicate IsSumDistinctSet transcribed byte-identically into lean/E1.lean from the estate copy of the formal-conjectures file
  OPERATION additive subset sum over the full powerset
  ARITH_FN subset_sum
  TARGET_LOCK LOCKED

TARGET_SHAPE TS0
  TARGET T0
  KIND EXISTENCE_OF_A_CONSTANT
  REQUIRED_COMPONENTS a single constant C > 0 valid for every n and every sum-distinct A
  CONTEXT_COMPONENTS the two variant declarations in the frozen file close nothing of the target
  CLOSURE_CRITERION a proof that there is a constant C > 0 with N >= C * 2 ^ n for every sum-distinct A subset of the interval one to N with cardinality n
  DOMAIN finite subsets A of the integer interval from one to N, cardinality n at least two
  COLLECTION_KIND SET
  DISTINCTNESS DISTINCT
  DEGENERATE_CASES empty A OUT, singleton A OUT
  DEGENERACY_FLOOR cardinality at least two
  LEAN_DEFAULTS the powerset includes the empty set and its sum is zero, so injectivity is over all two-to-the-n subsets
  BINDER_PREFIX there exists C positive, for all n, for all N, for all A
  POLARITY AFFIRMS
  DIRECTION LOWER
  QUANTIFIED_OVER MIN_OVER_CONFIGS
  NORMALIZATION the bound is on N, the ambient interval endpoint, not on the sum of A
  ANCHOR the least N admitting a three-element sum-distinct set is four

SOURCE_BIND S1
  SOURCE E1
  SYMBOL interval_endpoint_N
  READS_AS the endpoint of the ambient interval, A is contained in the integer interval one to N
  DISTINCT_FROM max_element_of_A
  WHY_DISTINCT a set with max A strictly below N satisfies the predicate for that N, so N is an upper bound on the largest element and not the largest element
  FINGERPRINT the Finset.Icc 1 N clause of IsSumDistinctSet in the frozen file

SOURCE_BIND S2
  SOURCE E1
  SYMBOL cardinality_of_A
  READS_AS the cardinality of A
  DISTINCT_FROM interval_endpoint_N
  WHY_DISTINCT they differ on every instance with cardinality below the interval length, which is every instance with n at least two
  FINGERPRINT the A.card occurrences in the frozen file

SOURCE_BIND S3
  SOURCE E1
  SYMBOL sum_distinct
  READS_AS the map sending a subset of A to the sum of its elements is injective on the entire powerset of A, the empty subset included
  DISTINCT_FROM Sidon
  WHY_DISTINCT a Sidon set only requires the pairwise sums to be distinct, and every three-element arithmetic progression separates the two classes
  FINGERPRINT the Injective clause of IsSumDistinctSet in the frozen file

CLOSE_CONTRACT CC1
  TARGET T0
  PROOF_REQUIRES a proof of a constant C > 0 with N >= C * 2 ^ n for every sum-distinct A of cardinality n inside the interval one to N
  DISPROOF_REQUIRES a proof that no positive constant works, that is a family of sum-distinct sets whose ratio N over two-to-the-n tends to zero
  NOT_CLOSURE STANDARD_FLOOR
  NOT_CLOSURE any bound carrying an n-dependent loss, in particular any bound of the form two-to-the-n over a positive power of n
  NOT_CLOSURE a bound on the sum of A rather than on the interval endpoint N
  FROZEN_WITH T0

