  ROUTE_KIND PROVE
  METHOD signed second moment over the powerset, then an integer spread count on the recentred sums
  FAMILY MOMENT_METHOD
  DIFFICULTY_DELTA KNOWN_THEOREM the loss against the target drops from a factor n to a factor root n, and the whole argument becomes elementary integer counting with no probability
  ROUTE_STATUS BLOCKED_CURRENT_TECHNIQUE
  BLOCKER the only facts used about A are that the two-to-the-n sums are distinct integers and that the sum of squares of the elements is at most n N squared, and those two facts are jointly satisfiable by a spread of order root n times N
